    "readmeMarkdown": "## Discord (third-party, pending review)\n\nRuns the **third-party** `@iqai/mcp-discord` server (IQAI) over stdio, pinned to `@0.0.6`. This is **not** an official Discord MCP server and is **pending PuPu review** (`needs_review`); the version is pinned so future releases are not auto-pulled without a re-vet. The bot token is read from the `DISCORD_TOKEN` environment variable, injected by the PuPu backend secret store \u2014 it is never written to localStorage.\n\n### Least-privilege bot setup (required)\n\nBefore connecting, create a **dedicated Discord bot** for the agent and grant it the **minimum** permissions only:\n\n- Do **not** grant the **Administrator** permission. Grant only the specific guild/channel permissions for the actions you want the agent to perform (e.g. Send Messages / Read Message History for the specific channels in use).\n- **Scope the bot to a single guild (server)** wherever possible, rather than inviting it to multiple servers.\n- When inviting the bot, select only the OAuth2 scopes/permissions it needs; avoid blanket permission integers.\n- Treat the bot token as a secret: rotate it if it leaks, and remove the bot from servers you no longer want the agent to reach.\n\nEvery write, messaging, moderation, webhook and login tool requires explicit confirmation; only read-only tools (get server info, read messages, list/get forum posts) run without a prompt."
  },
